
sloctl

Manage Nobl9 resources from the command line.

Commands that access Nobl9 use the active configuration context. Use --context
to select another context for one command, or --no-config-file to authenticate
with environment variables only.

Usage

sloctl [command]

Available Commands

• apply: Apply Nobl9 resource definitions
• aws-iam-ids: Get AWS IAM role identifiers
• budgetadjustments: Manage budget adjustment events
• completion: Generate shell completion scripts
• config: Manage sloctl configuration contexts
• convert: Convert external definitions to Nobl9 resources
• delete: Delete Nobl9 resources by name or definition file
• edit: Edit Nobl9 resources in the configured editor
• get: Get Nobl9 resources
• help: Help about any command
• mcp: Start the Nobl9 MCP proxy over stdio
• move: Move SLOs between Projects or Services
• replay: Replay historical SLI data for existing SLOs
• review: Manage SLO review
• validate: Validate SLI queries
• version: Print build and runtime version information

Flags

      --config string    Path to config.toml. If unset, use
                         SLOCTL_CONFIG_FILE_PATH or the platform default.
  -c, --context string   Use this context instead of the configured default for
                         the selected command.
  -h, --help             Help for sloctl.
      --no-config-file   For API authentication, use SLOCTL_CLIENT_ID and
                         SLOCTL_CLIENT_SECRET without reading or creating
                         config.toml. Configuration commands still access the
                         file.

Use sloctl [command] --help for more information about a command.
